00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.340 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  and manga and today we have a review of  the second episode of fire force the  heart of a fire soldier and it's safe to  say that this is not really what I was  expecting from a second installment  after last week's very action focused  first outing but I very much enjoyed  what episode 2 delivered because it was  such a stark contrast and demonstrated  that hey this series could actually be  capable of some decent emotional depth  and I'm really glad that fire force took  this turn so early on because I feel  like it was important to highlight the  humanity of the infernals rather than  continuing to see them as  monster-of-the-week sort of threats for  too much longer I mean in my review of  the first episode even I called them  fire demon II things and that term  greatly oversimplifies matters it makes  it quite easy to see them disposed of  whereas in this episode dealing with the  infernal was such a painful and  heartbreaking experience because what  they're forced to do is essentially  euthanize someone and of course the  whole episode very much centers around  this idea that company 8 are not some  sort of special combative unit but more  of a group who are expected to perform  this incredibly emotionally draining job  and implement actions that nobody else  can or should ever be expected to do and  once again this was absolutely not what  I was expecting even when they arrived  at the scene and everything was all  quiet I was still thinking that things  were going to get out of hand and very  destructive very quickly and then we cut  to the infernal sitting politely at the  table which was actually quite funny for  a second because at that moment my only  experience with these things were  violent and energetic however the true  tragedy of the situation struck me very  shortly after it was incredibly simple  but super impactful and I feel like this  specific case is something that's going  to carry over with me to future infernal  cases because from here on out I can't  think of them as anything but  exceptionally tragic humans so things  are getting very interesting from a  moral perspective and that was also  highlighted by the whole idea of keeping  your weapons concealed in public and  through the extended shots of the  victims daughter very very well done our  last tragedy is not the only focus of  this episode though because we also have  the introduction of Arthur Boyle who  seems to be the rival character for  Shinra and he brought a lot of fun stuff  to the table including some great comedy  that was sorely needed to balance this  episode out I have to say that initially  I am much more intrigued by his overall  design and character than I am generous  though although a lot of that may have  to do with the fact that you know almost  any character who wields a sword let  alone a plasma blade automatically  skyrockets in terms of favorability with  me and also after only one episode I  don't feel like I've had the proper time  to really bond in any way with Shinra I  mean yes we've seen a glimpse of his  tragic  but just over 20 minutes of screen time  isn't enough to stop another protagonist  type from swimming in and capturing a  bit more of my interest and Arthur game  into things very quickly so quickly that  I really hated the opening of this  episode because he just appeared right  in front of Shinra and a conflict of  sorts started to it Shinra seems to yell  and then promptly get cut off as the  opening credits begin playing which and  I cannot emphasize this enough was  jarring as hell I honestly think it's  one of the worst pieces of editing or  direction that I have ever seen and I  don't mean the whole opening sequence a  lot of it was quite beautiful I just  mean the cut to the opening credits this  just is not how you start an episode or  how you do anything it was just so  jarring and off-putting I feel like a  much better way to have gone about it  would have been to have Arthur appear  before Shinra then cut to the close-up  of him saying yo devil or even after he  says that he's here to slay a devil and  then hit the opening credits cutting  shinra's hole bit about taking it  outside altogether or finding a way to  include it after the opening maybe  because it simply does not work the way  it's presented and it is a huge stain on  this otherwise fantastic episode and  getting into more of said fantastic  episode there was a brilliant fight  sequence featuring Maki absolutely  owning both of our rookies which I  really appreciated  primarily because it showed off her  pyrokinetic abilities which I was very  curious about last week and it was just  great to see her kick some ass and there  was a nice bit of comedy in there with  the whole ogre thing and she just seems  like a nicely rounded character at this  stage fun to watch great in action and  cool abilities what more can I ask for I  am particularly intrigued by her power  should provide flames of what appears to  be some sort of sentience I don't think  it was explained in the episode maybe it  was and I just missed it but it was an  absurd the cool power and it makes me  wonder if she could do the same to  greater levels and quantities of flames  and you know essentially crafted  Godzilla scale fire dude bro that is  completely under her control suppose  we'll find out there was also a tiny bit  more if he namah this week and I'm still  not entirely sold on him he's just so  damn intense that intensity is played  for some decent laughs SIA and so I'm  looking forward to learning more about  exactly what his deal is the star of  this week to me though was definitely  Aki taro and his constant display of  competent leadership despite having no  fun fire related abilities he strikes me  as by far the most important member of  company eight due to his supreme  decision-making and ability to easily  read and interact with people the latter  of which is a heavily underrated trait  and one that I don't think any other  member of company 8 has because they all  seem to have that one feature that gets  them into some sort of conflict whether  it be serious or comical mainly comical  at this stage  but stuff like he knows extreme  seriousness Oh monkeys foolishness and  tendency to overreacted certain words or  even the lack of life experience of  Shinra and offer they all make  interacting with others difficult at  times and a Qatari seems to have that  special something that allows him to  easily read people and situations very  enviable I wish I had anything even  remotely resembling that kind of  awareness and judgment next up we were  also given hints of a greater evil this  week with the introduction of the guy  face whether he's a legitimate big bad  or some sort of lesser bad I have no  real opinion or inclination to guess on  right now but he has a cool enough  design I suppose kind of like a phallic  card from Helsing and cross from D  Grayman at a secret anime love child but  finally this episode also drops the  concept of the rookie fire soldier games  which smells an awful lot to me like the  beginnings of a classic shown in  tournament at the moment I suppose I'm  picturing something kind of like the  Sports Festival in my hero academia but  this should be a lot of fun if only for  the fact that I imagine we'll be getting  to meet a whole ton of characters from  other companies which is great because  I'm two episodes in and I'm already very  very eager to explore this expanded  build in a bit more depth and get a feel  for what other kinds of people are out  there as well that's what they're  capable of video look in essence episode  2 has me even more sold on this series  than the premiere last week it is shown  that fire force isn't necessarily at its  best with big over-the-top flame written  action pieces but that it can also  handle quiet and powerful moments with  incredible impact and as a result I will  be eagerly awaiting next week but that  pretty much does it for episode 2 of  fire force if you enjoyed this video  when the content this channel produce in  general then please do consider donating  to the new world review patreon because  the support of all of your amazing  people is what continues to make this  channel possible and if patreon isn't  quite your style then please do leave  this video a like share or subscribe  because it also helps support this  channel an incredible amount and if  you'd like to join the fun at any time  then please do head over to my discord  server where a wide array of shenanigan  ori takes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts on the episode this has been  the new world review and I'll see you  next time

